  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercisce_type\": \"CEFR Englished Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"readang_text\": \"\\\\\nIn the early hours of a crisp autumn morning, I decided to embark on an adventure through the dense forest near my village. The sun was just beginning its ascent over the horizon, casting long shadows that danced along the path before me. As I walked deeper into the woodland, I felt a sense of peace and tranquility wash over me. The rustling leaves underfoot were like an eerie lullaby, while birds chirped softly in the trees above.\\\\\n\\\\\nAfter about half an hour, I stumbled upon a small clearing where several old oak trees stood like guardians of time. At its center was a pond shimmering under the morning light; it looked as if someone had poured pure gold into nature's embrace. I sat down by the water's edge, feeling infinitely content with my surroundings.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What was the narrator's motivation for going into the forest?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"To attend a meeting\",\n        \"For a hiking adventure\",\n        \"To collect fruits and nuts\",\n        \"To visit friends\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"For a hiking adventure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"How did the narrator describe their feelings upon entering the forest?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Excited and eager\",\n        \"Panicked and confused\",\n        \"Peaceful and calm\",\n        \"Envious and disappointed\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"Peaceful and calm\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What was the narrator's reaction to finding a pond in the clearing?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"They felt restless and uneasy\",\n        \"They were shocked by its beauty\",\n        \"They decided to leave immediately\",\n        \"They felt no emotion\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"They were shocked by its beauty\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What imagery was used to describe the pond?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It looked like a mirror\",\n        \"It glittered as if made of glass\",\n        \"It shimmered like pure gold\",\n        \"It was dark and murky\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It shimmered like pure gold\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the author's attitude towards nature from this passage?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"They have never been happy\",\n        \"They are disconnected with the environment\",\n        \"They find peace and contentment in nature\",\n        \"They prefer urban settings\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"They find peace and contentment in nature\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
